# .clinerules — Mission 4: Mobile-First To-Do App

## 1. Architecture
- Vanilla stack ONLY: Semantic HTML5, Modular CSS3 (custom properties), Modern ES6+ JavaScript.
- No frameworks, no build step, no heavy external libraries. No CDNs unless strictly required.
- Single-page, single-responsibility files: `index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`.

## 2. Design Standards
- Mobile-first, optimized for 375px–430px viewports; scales cleanly to tablet/desktop via `min-width` media queries.
- Touch-friendly targets: minimum 44px tap area for every interactive control.
- Modern card styling, refined typography, consistent 8px spacing rhythm.
- Smooth, GPU-friendly CSS transitions (transform/opacity) for state toggles, deletions, and list changes.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Visible focus states for accessibility.

## 3. Code Quality
- Clean, small, single-purpose modular functions.
- Centralized state management: one `state` object is the single source of truth.
- Event delegation on containers — never bind per-item listeners.
- Strict input sanitization: never inject raw user input via `innerHTML`; build nodes or escape.
- Resilient `localStorage` persistence wrapped in try/catch with safe fallbacks.
- Zero memory leaks: no orphaned timers/listeners.

## 4. Execution Style
- Ship complete, production-ready code.
- Zero placeholders, zero `TODO`s, zero truncated snippets.
- Direct, concise communication. Maximum action.
